{"id": "EUVD-2026-76477", "enisaUuid": "0eeae891-7d87-39b0-bb95-66d06e035bef", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\njbd2: check need_resched() when skipping busy checkpoint buffers\n\njournal_shrink_one_cp_list() skips busy checkpoint buffers when called\nwith JBD2_SHRINK_BUSY_SKIP.  The continue statement on this path also\nskips the need_resched() check at the end of the loop body.\n\nConsequently, when a checkpoint list contains mostly busy buffers, the\nshrinker can walk the entire list while holding journal->j_list_lock,\neven when a reschedule has been requested.  Large checkpoint lists under\nmemory pressure can therefore cause long lock hold times and leave other\nCPUs spinning on j_list_lock, resulting in soft lockups or RCU stalls.\n\nRoute the busy-buffer path through the need_resched() check so that the\nshrinker can release j_list_lock and reschedule promptly, restoring\nparity with the clean-buffer path, which already checks need_resched().\nThis does not change which checkpoint buffers are eligible for removal.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc7ece0b827fe3b748db685fb85cd2fc3710c3f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f83c23286e54180cdc83a36463a60003534cc290", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9182a85991a0ad5cd2940df6db75f40ad90028c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/595cac7f1b32d009b97f83dd2b2d6a1a445e9bb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f213e12ff5c9590b1034ae8da0e6d09665c772d0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89566", "GHSA-p6jx-2fv3-6j26"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1ae4870f-06b0-3390-b721-159a3f7adf09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b98dba273a0e47dbfade89c9af73c5b012a4eabb <dc7ece0b827fe3b748db685fb85cd2fc3710c3f9"}, {"id": "1c336ff6-456f-3268-913a-eab9fc4154d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2600b81c-f2ce-38e2-bbb1-15f3a5e29c9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fda50e262e65bd553ff777c4b280afd1495a18b"}, {"id": "42591341-97aa-3352-a05f-68b22cf7b4b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "43bb7082-7692-37b5-a7c3-cede84842654", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5"}, {"id": "605be8c4-fcfa-3f67-9244-fe7489df773e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b98dba273a0e47dbfade89c9af73c5b012a4eabb <f213e12ff5c9590b1034ae8da0e6d09665c772d0"}, {"id": "63211794-4791-3334-bc70-cb13d8f6b1b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "557fda9ed70ebf8eda2620ba3d746215285a1303"}, {"id": "7166a235-178f-3c09-82c8-e36f9212f343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "78237ada-ba10-374f-b665-c861f281c6e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b98dba273a0e47dbfade89c9af73c5b012a4eabb <595cac7f1b32d009b97f83dd2b2d6a1a445e9bb4"}, {"id": "8a759fd5-c8cf-3e03-87a8-86cf0f10cb10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.129 <5.16"}, {"id": "9c488a8a-a739-3046-ab95-dd14a3f8d93c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.50 <6.2"}, {"id": "a72fd8a8-e850-38a0-b434-66ddfcbcb929", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "adffb224-fea5-3d0e-82ce-a262b585a802", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ae590a42-51c7-3bd4-9c79-c9279baf303b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b98dba273a0e47dbfade89c9af73c5b012a4eabb <f83c23286e54180cdc83a36463a60003534c